1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,133
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:40,333
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:42,633
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:46,467
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,267 --> 00:00:56,633
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:57,367 --> 00:00:59,233
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:00,633
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:02,000
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,167 --> 00:01:03,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:06,900
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,467
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,167
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:18,933
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,167 --> 00:01:21,500
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:24,600
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,233 --> 00:01:28,267
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:31,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:34,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,000
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:37,433
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:37,533 --> 00:01:38,800
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:38,900 --> 00:01:40,667
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:46,800
<i>Earlier, someone knocked
on the door.</i>

24
00:01:46,900 --> 00:01:49,033
- They left this parcel outside.
<i> - What's inside?</i>

25
00:01:49,167 --> 00:01:52,333
- A mission. It's a job for me.
<i> - What kind of mission?</i>

26
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:54,800
<i>Hunting down people
who have broken the law.</i>

27
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:58,533
<i>- How much are we talking?
- One hundred thousand pesos.</i>

28
00:01:58,667 --> 00:02:01,700
<i>So, why is my youngest
always in a hurry?</i>

29
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:04,333
<i>We're handling a huge case
in NCIA.</i>

30
00:02:04,433 --> 00:02:05,733
<i> It's a gold smuggling case.</i>

31
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:10,033
<i>Oh, Ricardo, you daughter here
is after a syndicate.</i>

32
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:11,333
<i> When I was her age,</i>

33
00:02:11,433 --> 00:02:13,533
<i>I had dealt
with more serious cases.</i>

34
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:15,467
She hasn't proven anything yet.

35
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,667
<i>Sure you're prepared?
Don't mess this up.</i>

36
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:19,933
<i>We're ready, ma'am.
Thank you for the confidence.</i>

37
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,567
<i> Let's move!</i>

38
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:23,400
<i> Pops. Gabo took the mission.</i>

39
00:02:23,533 --> 00:02:26,033
<i>The real question is,
will he do it?</i>

40
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:27,567
<i> Give him some time.</i>

41
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:31,867
<i>I have strong faith that
Gabo will carry out the mission.</i>

42
00:02:35,367 --> 00:02:37,700
Why do the two of you
look like that?

43
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:42,567
It's Chinese New Year.
We're going to Chinatown.

44
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:46,067
[LAWIN] We'll check out
what Gabo will do.

45
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:47,700
- Checkmate.
- That's it.

46
00:02:47,833 --> 00:02:48,767
Huh?

47
00:02:49,467 --> 00:02:50,367
[CHESS PIECE CLINKS]

48
00:02:50,467 --> 00:02:51,933
[PAPANG CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

49
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,700
[VAN DOOR SLIDING]

50
00:02:57,167 --> 00:02:58,467
Boss.

51
00:02:58,633 --> 00:03:00,100
[VAN DOOR SLIDES, CLOSES]

52
00:03:00,233 --> 00:03:01,433
I'll feel them out first.

53
00:03:01,567 --> 00:03:03,600
If I get to explain it
to them well...

54
00:03:04,767 --> 00:03:06,433
I'll tell you
if you can go upstairs.

55
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:09,567
Just find a way
to interview them!

56
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:11,600
Remember, your careers
are at stake here!

57
00:03:11,767 --> 00:03:12,733
Yes, boss.

58
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:15,600
Salvador. You take care of it.

59
00:03:16,333 --> 00:03:17,600
And do it well!

60
00:03:17,733 --> 00:03:23,100
Do it well? And if you forget
to record it again,

61
00:03:23,300 --> 00:03:24,967
I might as well just forget you.

62
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,600
Yes, boss.
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

63
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:29,800
Come on, let's go.
Fix your equipment.

64
00:03:29,933 --> 00:03:32,300
[SALVADOR] Sir. Sir!

65
00:03:32,433 --> 00:03:33,967
Oh, oh? Oh?

66
00:03:35,467 --> 00:03:37,633
You're Rudy's
brother-in-law, right?

67
00:03:37,767 --> 00:03:38,800
Yeah.

68
00:03:38,967 --> 00:03:41,067
You're the one
who interviewed Betchay, right?

69
00:03:41,167 --> 00:03:45,667
- Have you released that yet?
- That's actually my problem.

70
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,267
W-Where's Betchay?

71
00:03:48,367 --> 00:03:51,300
Oh, they went home.

72
00:03:51,833 --> 00:03:53,167
They went back
to Ginintuang Lupa.

73
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:55,300
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,433
[TEKLA] Gabo!

75
00:03:56,533 --> 00:03:58,000
- [DOOR CREAKS]
- [KNOCKS ON DOOR]

76
00:03:58,167 --> 00:03:59,500
Gabo!

77
00:03:59,667 --> 00:04:01,500
- [GABO] I'm getting dressed!
- Oh, he's getting dressed.

78
00:04:01,633 --> 00:04:03,500
Do they have food?
I'm starving.

79
00:04:03,667 --> 00:04:05,200
You haven't eaten breakfast?

80
00:04:05,367 --> 00:04:06,533
You're always hungry.

81
00:04:06,700 --> 00:04:07,833
Hey, don't touch those.

82
00:04:07,967 --> 00:04:09,133
[WATER TRICKLING]

83
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,667
- There! A can of sardines!
- [QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

84
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,167
Oh, there's bread!
The perfect pair!

85
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:14,367
- Perfect pair!
- Hey! Hey!

86
00:04:14,533 --> 00:04:15,500
You guys are shameless.

87
00:04:15,633 --> 00:04:16,667
Hey, don't touch that.

88
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:18,167
Auntie Betchay will get pissed.

89
00:04:18,333 --> 00:04:20,167
Just a few bites, man.
It's just food.

90
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:21,533
I hear you, it's just food.

91
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,700
But I'm telling you,
you won't like her mad.

92
00:04:24,867 --> 00:04:26,967
He's right.
You'll get Gabo in trouble.

93
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:29,000
I'm starving.
I haven't eaten breakfast.

94
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,833
Don't you feel bad for him?

95
00:04:31,567 --> 00:04:33,467
- Put it in the bowl.
- Breakfast.

96
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:35,233
We've warned you.

97
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,033
- Dig in.
- [TEKLA] Leave me out of that.

98
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:39,300
- Gabo.
- What's up.

99
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,467
- What?
- Eat with us, Gabo.

100
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:43,200
- Oh, Gabo.
- [CUTLERY CLANKS]

101
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:47,300
You guys should go.

102
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,567
I have to pass by the hospital.

103
00:04:48,733 --> 00:04:50,300
I need to check on Papa.

104
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,000
Oh, we'll come with you.

105
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:53,533
No need.

106
00:04:53,700 --> 00:04:55,467
Let's just meet in Chinatown.

107
00:04:55,567 --> 00:04:57,400
- I'll be there.
- Okay.

108
00:04:57,567 --> 00:04:58,533
We'll go there now.

109
00:04:58,700 --> 00:05:00,033
For sure, it'll be packed today.

110
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:01,367
It's Chinese New Year.

111
00:05:01,567 --> 00:05:02,867
Perfect!

112
00:05:02,967 --> 00:05:05,067
Chinese people will be
giving out red envelopes!

113
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:06,567
- Exactly
- Mm-hmm.

114
00:05:06,733 --> 00:05:08,267
- Come on.
- Be careful, okay?

115
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,667
Be discreet so that the person
doesn't get suspicious.

116
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:14,067
Come on, let's move.
We might miss them.

117
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:15,233
- Come on.
- Okay, then.

118
00:05:15,367 --> 00:05:17,333
- Hurry.
- Grab this one!

119
00:05:17,433 --> 00:05:18,900
[TEKLA] Hey, don't bring food!

120
00:05:19,067 --> 00:05:21,067
All you guys do is eat.
You guys are shameless.

121
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,367
Oh, it's Auntie Betchay.

122
00:05:23,467 --> 00:05:24,900
Auntie Betchay.

123
00:05:25,067 --> 00:05:27,400
- [BETCHAY] Oh.
- How's Uncle Rudy?

124
00:05:27,533 --> 00:05:29,400
He's still not well.
He is in the ICU.

125
00:05:29,567 --> 00:05:31,233
Have you seen Gabo?

126
00:05:31,367 --> 00:05:32,933
Oh, he's at home.

127
00:05:34,933 --> 00:05:35,733
What's that?

128
00:05:35,833 --> 00:05:38,233
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

129
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:40,067
Did you get food from our home?

130
00:05:41,167 --> 00:05:42,433
See? I told you.

131
00:05:42,567 --> 00:05:45,367
That's enough!
We've got a much bigger problem.

132
00:05:45,467 --> 00:05:46,633
I only grabbed one!

133
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,933
We really need
to get this job done.

134
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,267
We can't fail, okay?

135
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,933
Uncle Rudy's life is at stake.

136
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:55,967
You three, don't fool around.

137
00:05:56,133 --> 00:05:59,267
Don't let Mr. Chan
get away or else!

138
00:05:59,567 --> 00:06:01,533
Why do you hate us three?

139
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:03,767
Take it easy!
We won't fail! Never!

140
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,100
- "Never"?
- Let's go.

141
00:06:05,267 --> 00:06:07,133
We might miss Mr. Chan.

142
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:09,067
Your breath stinks.
I think you're hungry. Here.

143
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:11,567
- Eat up.
- [TEKLA] Leave me out of it.

144
00:06:12,167 --> 00:06:13,933
I knew it!

145
00:06:14,033 --> 00:06:16,967
- They even ate my sardines!
- [GLASS BOWL BREAKS]

146
00:06:17,333 --> 00:06:19,967
Hey, calm down! It's just food!

147
00:06:20,133 --> 00:06:21,433
"Just food"?!

148
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:23,167
That's exactly it!

149
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:24,933
It's food!

150
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:27,433
We can't afford to buy medicine!

151
00:06:27,533 --> 00:06:29,633
We can't afford
to pay hospital bills!

152
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:31,300
Does that not make you frantic?!

153
00:06:31,433 --> 00:06:33,067
- Oh, please--
- I am so tired!

154
00:06:33,167 --> 00:06:35,633
I'm so tired because it's always
been my responsibility!

155
00:06:35,767 --> 00:06:37,300
It's always been me!

156
00:06:37,433 --> 00:06:38,567
You're making
the situation worse--

157
00:06:38,667 --> 00:06:40,833
I'm making it worse?!

158
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,267
You think I'm making it worse?!

159
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:46,033
Oh really, Mameng?

160
00:06:46,533 --> 00:06:48,433
My goodness!

161
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,967
So now I'm making it worse.

162
00:06:51,633 --> 00:06:52,867
Gosh. Argh! [TAPS LOUDLY]

163
00:06:53,833 --> 00:06:55,867
Whatever. If you don't--

164
00:07:00,133 --> 00:07:01,267
Damn it.

165
00:07:01,367 --> 00:07:02,833
Of course it won't start

166
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,500
right when the owner
picks it up.

167
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:06,000
This is bad.

168
00:07:06,833 --> 00:07:08,033
What could be the problem?

169
00:07:09,867 --> 00:07:12,133
[MOTORCYCLE ENGINE STARTS, DIES]

170
00:07:12,233 --> 00:07:13,300
Oh, Badong.

171
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:14,767
- Badong.
- Oh, Elton.

172
00:07:14,900 --> 00:07:17,533
Man, you know a lot
about motorcycles, right?

173
00:07:18,267 --> 00:07:20,667
I've been trying to fix this,
but the engine dies.

174
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:23,333
The owner, who's a seaman,
will pick it up today.

175
00:07:23,433 --> 00:07:24,533
Can you help us?

176
00:07:24,667 --> 00:07:26,000
We desperately need
the money right now.

177
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:28,033
Sure, Elton.
I'll try my best.

178
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:30,567
We really need the money
to pay the bills.

179
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,700
Here are the tools.

180
00:07:36,567 --> 00:07:38,800
[BETCHAY]
Well, Gabo? Where is it?

181
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,533
Where's the promise you made?

182
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,900
You said you were going
to find a way

183
00:07:44,067 --> 00:07:45,667
to have your father
undergo surgery.

184
00:07:45,767 --> 00:07:47,133
Now, where is it? Tell me!

185
00:07:47,233 --> 00:07:48,200
[MAMENG] Hey!

186
00:07:48,367 --> 00:07:50,533
Don't talk to Gabo like that!

187
00:07:50,633 --> 00:07:51,667
[BETCHAY] And why not?

188
00:07:51,767 --> 00:07:53,333
It's the truth!

189
00:07:53,633 --> 00:07:54,900
I only told the truth!

190
00:07:55,033 --> 00:07:56,733
You made a promise, remember?

191
00:07:56,867 --> 00:08:00,000
Didn't you say
you'd do whatever it takes

192
00:08:00,100 --> 00:08:02,667
to get your father
operated on?!

193
00:08:02,767 --> 00:08:04,367
So, what happened?

194
00:08:04,467 --> 00:08:05,567
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

195
00:08:05,733 --> 00:08:07,167
I've got a job, Auntie.

196
00:08:07,967 --> 00:08:09,000
What?

197
00:08:10,433 --> 00:08:11,400
A job?

198
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,367
You have a job? Is it true?

199
00:08:14,467 --> 00:08:15,733
What kind of job is it?

200
00:08:16,700 --> 00:08:18,267
I have to look for someone.

201
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,100
After that, I'll get paid.

202
00:08:20,267 --> 00:08:22,233
- [BETCHAY SCOFFING]
- It's in Chinatown.

203
00:08:22,433 --> 00:08:24,733
More nonsense again, huh?

204
00:08:24,833 --> 00:08:26,967
Who are you planning
to kill this time?

205
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:30,533
Tell us so we can be prepared.

206
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:32,800
That way, we won't get
a headache

207
00:08:32,967 --> 00:08:34,767
worrying about
how to help you

208
00:08:34,933 --> 00:08:36,700
avoid getting locked up again!

209
00:08:36,800 --> 00:08:38,067
- Your father--
- Shh!

210
00:08:38,167 --> 00:08:39,267
Enough!

211
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:40,400
Come on, dear.

212
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:41,533
- Don't listen to her.
- Argh!

213
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:42,700
She's crazy.

214
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,433
Come on, look.
I'll take care of it.

215
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:46,567
I'll look after your father.

216
00:08:46,667 --> 00:08:48,433
Your job is important.

217
00:08:48,600 --> 00:08:50,100
Focus on that.
It's going to be alright.

218
00:08:50,267 --> 00:08:53,533
Listen, concentrate on your job.
That's what matters.

219
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:55,700
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

220
00:08:55,833 --> 00:08:57,133
[MAMENG] But, Gabo...

221
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,300
Promise me one thing.

222
00:09:00,433 --> 00:09:03,100
You wouldn't do
anything stupid, alright?

223
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:09,967
I promise, Auntie.

224
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:11,833
Be careful.

225
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:18,667
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

226
00:09:18,833 --> 00:09:20,800
- [ENGINE STARTS]
- [ELTON] Good job, Badong!

227
00:09:21,500 --> 00:09:23,333
You got it running! Awesome!

228
00:09:24,333 --> 00:09:25,733
Man, you're amazing!

229
00:09:26,633 --> 00:09:27,833
- Whoo!
- Nice engine, Elton.

230
00:09:28,033 --> 00:09:29,500
Of course, it's brand new!

231
00:09:29,633 --> 00:09:30,867
Rudy even assembled it himself!

232
00:09:31,033 --> 00:09:34,333
You know what?
Help me fix this car.

233
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,767
We can use the payment
for Rudy's hospital bills.

234
00:09:36,867 --> 00:09:37,800
[KEYS JINGLING]

235
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:40,167
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:09:40,333 --> 00:09:41,833
I've been working on it
for three days,

237
00:09:41,967 --> 00:09:43,000
but it just won't start.

238
00:09:43,167 --> 00:09:46,467
I think the distributor is
the problem.

239
00:09:46,567 --> 00:09:47,967
Or maybe it's the carburetor.

240
00:09:48,067 --> 00:09:49,933
- Okay, I'll check it out.
- Thanks.

241
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:51,833
Take over.
I'll check the back.

242
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,500
There's a problem there too.

243
00:09:53,667 --> 00:10:00,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

244
00:10:15,033 --> 00:10:18,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

245
00:10:18,500 --> 00:10:19,900
[TARP RUSTLES, FLAPPING]

246
00:10:20,067 --> 00:10:27,033
[THRILLING MUSIC PLAYING]

247
00:10:42,033 --> 00:10:49,033
[THRILLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

248
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,900
[OLI] Uh, good morning.

249
00:10:53,067 --> 00:10:54,100
- Yes?
- Can I ask a question?

250
00:10:54,267 --> 00:10:56,400
- Where do the Magtibays live?
- [ENGINE STARTS]

251
00:10:56,533 --> 00:10:59,400
[ENGINE ROARING]

252
00:10:59,567 --> 00:11:01,233
- [WOMAN] That's their house.
- Oh, that one?

253
00:11:01,400 --> 00:11:02,233
Badong!

254
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:04,267
- Who snatched the motorcycle?
- No clue!

255
00:11:04,433 --> 00:11:06,500
Then how will we get paid?
Let's catch him!

256
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,733
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

257
00:11:08,933 --> 00:11:15,967
[ENGINE REVVING]

258
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,100
[ENGINE ROARS]

259
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,300
[HEAVY THUD]

260
00:11:23,767 --> 00:11:25,400
- Good day!
- Good day!

261
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,400
- Good day!
- Anyone home?

262
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:30,467
- Anyone home?
- Anyone home? Oh.

263
00:11:30,467 --> 00:11:32,333
[SALVADOR] Good day, ma'am.

264
00:11:32,333 --> 00:11:34,233
You guys again?

265
00:11:34,233 --> 00:11:36,233
[SALVADOR] We'd just like
to interview you again.

266
00:11:36,233 --> 00:11:39,233
Our executive producer,
Boss Arnel, is here with us.

267
00:11:39,233 --> 00:11:42,100
Why? Is there a problem?
Did I say something wrong?

268
00:11:42,133 --> 00:11:44,267
No, it's not that.
We liked it.

269
00:11:44,267 --> 00:11:48,200
Your response was great
and full of emotions but...

270
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:49,233
But what?

271
00:11:50,467 --> 00:11:53,667
We failed to record
the interview.

272
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:55,267
Oh, my goodness.

273
00:11:55,267 --> 00:11:57,367
Do you even know how
to do your job?

274
00:11:57,367 --> 00:11:58,633
Unbelievable!

275
00:11:58,633 --> 00:12:01,633
We're busy enough as it is,
and you're still bothering us?

276
00:12:01,633 --> 00:12:07,433
We'd like to do a feature on how
policemen abuse their power.

277
00:12:07,433 --> 00:12:09,667
Your husband was shot,

278
00:12:09,667 --> 00:12:12,767
and filing charges will
help the case a lot.

279
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:17,100
We can even provide
a lawyer for you.

280
00:12:18,467 --> 00:12:20,633
[WHISPERING] Here.
Give this to them.

281
00:12:20,633 --> 00:12:21,467
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

282
00:12:21,467 --> 00:12:25,167
Please consider this
as our help.

283
00:12:25,167 --> 00:12:27,467
We hope this will do.

284
00:12:27,467 --> 00:12:31,500
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

285
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:35,433
This isn't enough to buy
antibiotics for Rudy.

286
00:12:36,467 --> 00:12:37,833
Oh, alright.

287
00:12:38,633 --> 00:12:40,767
Here. Take this, too.

288
00:12:42,367 --> 00:12:43,833
Will that be enough?

289
00:12:43,833 --> 00:12:46,367
Where do you want to
do the interview? Come inside.

290
00:12:46,367 --> 00:12:48,200
- Over there.
- There? Okay.

291
00:12:48,233 --> 00:12:49,733
- Come in.
- [OLI] Okay, thank you.

292
00:12:49,733 --> 00:12:52,567
- Thank you so much.
- We're going inside.

293
00:12:52,567 --> 00:12:53,700
Thank you.

294
00:12:54,767 --> 00:12:56,667
The people of Ginintuang
Lupa filed

295
00:12:56,667 --> 00:12:58,333
a temporary restraining order
against us.

296
00:12:58,333 --> 00:13:00,833
Then file a counter
restraining order.

297
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:03,733
Call our contacts
in the judiciary

298
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:05,900
and make sure the decision
turns in our favor.

299
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:08,833
- It's as simple as that.
- Okay. I'll do that, sir.

300
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:10,333
Manny.

301
00:13:10,333 --> 00:13:15,833
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:13:15,833 --> 00:13:20,000
I'm a Jacinto.
I have money and power.

303
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:23,267
We won't stop until
we kick out

304
00:13:23,300 --> 00:13:24,900
all those squatters
in Ginintuang Lupa.

305
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:25,867
Yes, sir.

306
00:13:31,867 --> 00:13:33,533
Oli, make sure you record it
this time, okay?

307
00:13:33,533 --> 00:13:36,233
Excuse me. I'll just go over
there and make some coffee.

308
00:13:36,233 --> 00:13:37,300
- Okay, thank you.
- Thank you.

309
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:39,033
- [MAMENG] Excuse me.
- [SALVADOR] Thank you.

310
00:13:39,033 --> 00:13:40,067
[OLI] Thanks.

311
00:13:40,067 --> 00:13:41,800
Oli, make sure you
get everything.

312
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:42,967
We can't make
any more mistakes.

313
00:13:42,967 --> 00:13:44,867
Yes, boss. I got this.

314
00:13:44,867 --> 00:13:47,533
- Or I'll have you fired.
- It's all good now.

315
00:13:47,533 --> 00:13:49,033
- [SALVADOR] Okay. Ready?
- [OLI] Okay.

316
00:13:49,033 --> 00:13:50,733
Rolling. Action!

317
00:13:50,733 --> 00:13:52,400
Uh, ma'am...

318
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:54,467
How have you been
holding up

319
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,967
after what happened
to Mister Rudy?

320
00:13:55,967 --> 00:13:57,400
He's still in the hospital--

321
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:58,767
- [THUD]
- Oh!

322
00:13:58,767 --> 00:14:00,567
- Ma'am.
- Sorry about that.

323
00:14:00,567 --> 00:14:02,933
We could hear you.
We're recording here.

324
00:14:02,933 --> 00:14:04,733
- Sorry. The lid was hot.
- Please keep it down.

325
00:14:04,733 --> 00:14:06,667
- Okay, again.
- Ready?

326
00:14:06,667 --> 00:14:07,500
[OLI] Okay, go.

327
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:08,900
- [ARNEL] Rolling.
- Okay, rolling.

328
00:14:08,900 --> 00:14:11,600
- Three, two, one. Action.
- Okay.

329
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,567
Ma'am, how have you been
holding up

330
00:14:14,567 --> 00:14:17,567
since your husband,
Mister Rudy, got shot?

331
00:14:18,267 --> 00:14:19,233
[IN STERN VOICE]
He's still at the hospital.

332
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:21,633
He's in the ICU
and has not woken up yet.

333
00:14:21,633 --> 00:14:23,900
- [QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]
- Wait, cut!

334
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:26,467
You sounded angry.

335
00:14:26,467 --> 00:14:28,400
Remember, your husband
is in the hospital.

336
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:30,600
Let your sadness out.
We need to show emotions.

337
00:14:30,600 --> 00:14:32,100
Talk to her.
Help bring out her emotions.

338
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:34,500
- Pull out her emotions.
- [SALVADOR] Look, ma'am.

339
00:14:34,500 --> 00:14:39,433
If you're angry, you won't get
sympathy from the viewers.

340
00:14:39,433 --> 00:14:44,367
Instead of anger,
express more of your sadness.

341
00:14:44,367 --> 00:14:46,833
I already gave you money, right?
Why are you still mad?

342
00:14:46,833 --> 00:14:48,600
- You get me?
- [OLI] Tug at people's hearts.

343
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,100
- Tug at their heartstrings.
- That's right.

344
00:14:50,100 --> 00:14:51,967
- [ARNEL] You ready, ma'am?
- [OLI] Are we good?

345
00:14:51,967 --> 00:14:53,467
- [ARNEL] Okay, rolling!
- Go.

346
00:14:53,467 --> 00:14:55,267
Three, two, one, action!

347
00:14:55,867 --> 00:14:57,633
Ma'am, how have you been

348
00:14:57,633 --> 00:15:00,433
since your husband,
Mister Rudy, got shot?

349
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:08,467
[COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]

350
00:15:08,467 --> 00:15:11,033
[VOICE SHAKING] My husband
is still at the hospital.

351
00:15:11,033 --> 00:15:13,733
He hasn't woken up yet.

352
00:15:13,733 --> 00:15:15,800
Ah, wait. Cut! Cut! Cut!

353
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:16,833
Let's do that again.

354
00:15:16,833 --> 00:15:19,700
Ma'am, your husband
is fighting for his life.

355
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:21,633
- Yeah!
- He's on the verge of death.

356
00:15:21,633 --> 00:15:22,700
He's dying.

357
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:27,967
We need to feel your sorrow
and your heartache.

358
00:15:27,967 --> 00:15:30,033
Put your heart into it.

359
00:15:30,033 --> 00:15:31,733
Give it your all!

360
00:15:31,733 --> 00:15:32,800
Salvador, motivate her.

361
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,867
- [SIGHS DEEPLY] Talk to her.
- Okay, okay.

362
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:37,733
[SALVADOR] Ma'am, listen.
Here's what you should do.

363
00:15:37,733 --> 00:15:41,367
Just imagine your husband
is going to die tomorrow.

364
00:15:41,367 --> 00:15:42,500
- [OLI] Right.
- [SALVADOR] Okay?

365
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:44,367
- You'll be a widow forever.
- What?!

366
00:15:44,367 --> 00:15:45,867
[SALVADOR]
No, just imagine it!

367
00:15:45,867 --> 00:15:47,567
And you don't have any money.

368
00:15:47,567 --> 00:15:49,600
- [ARNEL] Yes, perfect.
- We really don't have money.

369
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,667
Yeah, but just think about it,

370
00:15:51,667 --> 00:15:54,500
so you can bring out
the right emotions.

371
00:15:54,500 --> 00:15:56,600
- That's it. Be natural.
- [OLI] That's good.

372
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:58,067
[ARNEL] If you can cry, do it.

373
00:15:58,067 --> 00:16:01,367
From 1 to 10, give us 10.
Yes, that's perfect.

374
00:16:01,367 --> 00:16:03,033
Give us a bigger frown.

375
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:04,700
- Roll camera!
- Looks like she's ready!

376
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:06,933
- Ready?
- Three, two, one, action!

377
00:16:06,933 --> 00:16:08,400
- Ma'am...
- [SOBBING SOFTLY]

378
00:16:08,433 --> 00:16:09,967
How have you been holding up

379
00:16:09,967 --> 00:16:12,433
since your husband,
Mister Rudy, got hurt?

380
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:16,933
[WAILS]

381
00:16:16,933 --> 00:16:21,133
We need your help!
We don't have any money!

382
00:16:21,133 --> 00:16:25,133
My husband's still confined!
He hasn't even woken up yet!

383
00:16:25,133 --> 00:16:27,567
- [SALVADOR] Good. Keep it up.
- [SOBS]

384
00:16:27,567 --> 00:16:29,767
We can't afford
his hospital bills!

385
00:16:29,767 --> 00:16:33,133
[SOBS LOUDLY] We don't know
what else to do!

386
00:16:33,133 --> 00:16:36,733
[BETCHAY CONTINUES TO WAIL]

387
00:16:36,733 --> 00:16:39,700
- [WAILS LOUDER]
- [WHISPERING] Get closer.

388
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:41,400
Close up on her face.

389
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,433
Rudy!

390
00:16:43,467 --> 00:16:45,567
- [MAMENG WAILS]
- Camera, film her!

391
00:16:45,567 --> 00:16:47,433
- My brother!
- Don't miss it!

392
00:16:47,433 --> 00:16:49,167
Focus on her! Come on!

393
00:16:49,167 --> 00:16:53,067
- Go film Mameng!
- Take me with you, Rudy!

394
00:16:53,067 --> 00:16:56,733
- [CRYING]
- What are you saying, ma'am?

395
00:16:56,733 --> 00:16:58,100
Hey!

396
00:16:58,100 --> 00:17:01,800
- Take you where?
- Don't leave me! [CRIES LOUDER]

397
00:17:01,800 --> 00:17:04,733
- [COMICAL MUSIC PLAYING]
- I'd rather die now...

398
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:08,933
- Go back to Betchay!
- ...than watch my husband die!

399
00:17:08,933 --> 00:17:11,633
- Please help us!
- [CONTINUES WAILING]

400
00:17:11,633 --> 00:17:13,833
- [SALVADOR] Wait, wait!
- I can't breathe!

401
00:17:13,833 --> 00:17:15,567
- Come here!
- Move over there!

402
00:17:15,600 --> 00:17:17,667
[MAMENG, BETCHAY WAILING]

403
00:17:17,667 --> 00:17:20,100
Bring her next to Mameng!
Help her walk!

404
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:22,967
Ma'am, I'm not your husband!
I'm not your husband!

405
00:17:22,967 --> 00:17:24,767
Wait, ma'am! Let go!

406
00:17:24,767 --> 00:17:26,700
- Please help my husband!
- My brother!

407
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:30,700
- My poor brother!
- Please have mercy on us!

408
00:17:30,700 --> 00:17:32,933
- Did you get that?
- [OLI] Yes, I got it all.

409
00:17:32,933 --> 00:17:34,167
Good take! That's enough.

410
00:17:36,133 --> 00:17:42,667
[ENGINE REVVS]

411
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:50,133
[ARNEL] Salvador.

412
00:17:51,333 --> 00:17:52,867
I'm telling you,

413
00:17:53,333 --> 00:17:57,633
make sure your report
has heart and feelings.

414
00:17:57,867 --> 00:17:59,700
To make the people
more interested!

415
00:18:00,233 --> 00:18:02,133
It's lacking!

416
00:18:02,467 --> 00:18:04,667
- Your report is lacking.
- You want me to overdo it?

417
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:06,667
I feel like I'm deceiving
the people.

418
00:18:06,667 --> 00:18:08,000
What do you mean
by deceiving?!

419
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,467
It's true that the police

420
00:18:09,467 --> 00:18:11,567
were the ones who shot
her husband.

421
00:18:11,567 --> 00:18:15,500
All we're doing is adding
more life to the interview!

422
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:17,400
Stand there.
Stand right there.

423
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,467
- Right here?
- Take a shot of him here.

424
00:18:19,467 --> 00:18:21,033
So people can see
how poor they are!

425
00:18:21,033 --> 00:18:22,900
- Alright!
- This angle right there.

426
00:18:22,933 --> 00:18:24,000
Right there!

427
00:18:24,433 --> 00:18:27,033
[OLI] Two... thee... take!

428
00:18:27,033 --> 00:18:29,200
After speaking with the lady,

429
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:32,933
one question still arises.

430
00:18:32,933 --> 00:18:36,333
One. How long will the law
protectors be held accountable?

431
00:18:36,333 --> 00:18:37,067
Second.

432
00:18:37,067 --> 00:18:38,533
Instead of peace,

433
00:18:38,533 --> 00:18:41,533
this operation left behind fear.

434
00:18:41,533 --> 00:18:46,100
Third. Instead of protection,
they all felt anxiety.

435
00:18:46,100 --> 00:18:47,900
The residents who have
already lost their homes

436
00:18:47,900 --> 00:18:49,567
may also risk losing
their loved ones.

437
00:18:50,533 --> 00:18:51,400
Right?

438
00:18:51,400 --> 00:18:52,433
Thank you.

439
00:18:52,433 --> 00:18:54,067
Be more aggressive!

440
00:18:54,067 --> 00:18:56,433
Let out your anger
towards the police!

441
00:18:56,467 --> 00:18:58,133
Don't be like that.
Be more aggressive!

442
00:18:58,133 --> 00:18:59,800
Like picking a fight?

443
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:02,067
That's not who I am.

444
00:19:02,067 --> 00:19:04,900
We need to show
how angry we are!

445
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,900
Find a way to do that, Salvador.

446
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:09,600
Let's find a way to show that
to the viewers!

447
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,733
You can't be like that!

448
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:14,400
- Make that happen.
- [OLI] Salvador, let's go.

449
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:16,233
- Cheers, sir!
- [OLI] Hey.

450
00:19:16,233 --> 00:19:17,333
[OLI] Salvador!

451
00:19:18,733 --> 00:19:21,733
- Is that clean?
- [MAN] Of course, it is!

452
00:19:21,733 --> 00:19:24,367
Just take a shot.
Here you go.

453
00:19:25,433 --> 00:19:27,700
You really are a scene-stealer.

454
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:29,400
Hey!

455
00:19:29,433 --> 00:19:30,767
I was just...

456
00:19:30,767 --> 00:19:34,500
I was wondering,
what if we really lose Rudy?

457
00:19:34,500 --> 00:19:37,233
He's my brother, of course,
I'd react that way!

458
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:38,700
[SIGHS]

459
00:19:39,433 --> 00:19:40,800
But, what do you think, huh?

460
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,933
Do you think
they'll really help us

461
00:19:43,300 --> 00:19:44,600
get a lawyer

462
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,900
so we can file
against the police?

463
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:50,933
You want to file
a case against them?

464
00:19:50,933 --> 00:19:52,133
Of course, I do!

465
00:19:52,133 --> 00:19:56,600
Shouldn't we seek justice
for what they've done to Rudy?

466
00:19:56,600 --> 00:20:00,300
Whoever did it should
be held accountable!

467
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,833
That would be a hassle.

468
00:20:02,867 --> 00:20:08,000
I'm sure they'll cover for
their fellow police officers.

469
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:11,133
It will just lead to nowhere!

470
00:20:11,133 --> 00:20:13,967
I thought you loved Rudy!

471
00:20:13,967 --> 00:20:17,967
Why don't you want
to seek justice for him?!

472
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:20,433
I love your brother so much!

473
00:20:20,433 --> 00:20:24,300
I also want the person
who shot him arrested!

474
00:20:24,300 --> 00:20:26,833
But if we file a case
against the police,

475
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:29,100
it's just like picking up a rock

476
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,933
and smashing it against
our own heads.

477
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,433
[CROWD CHEERING]

478
00:20:35,467 --> 00:20:36,800
[ARNEL] That's enough.
Let's get back to work!

479
00:20:37,867 --> 00:20:40,367
[CROWD CHEERING]

480
00:20:40,733 --> 00:20:43,900
[ARNEL] That's enough.
Let's get back to work!

481
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:45,033
There you go, sir!

482
00:20:45,033 --> 00:20:46,333
- [OLI] Are you okay?
- [ARNEL] Are you okay?

483
00:20:46,333 --> 00:20:47,967
- Yes!
- Alright, let's go!

484
00:20:47,967 --> 00:20:48,867
Okay, okay.

485
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:50,200
[OLI] Please, step aside.

486
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:52,300
- [SALVADOR] Let me speak.
- Do a good job.

487
00:20:52,300 --> 00:20:55,133
Three, two, one... action!

488
00:20:55,133 --> 00:20:58,500
After interviewing
the woman whose husband

489
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,367
is currently in critical
condition at the hospital,

490
00:21:00,367 --> 00:21:03,100
following a demolition
that was supposed to be peaceful

491
00:21:03,833 --> 00:21:06,000
led by the police.

492
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:09,967
A huge question now looms
over the family.

493
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:13,533
Who shot him? Who?

494
00:21:13,533 --> 00:21:15,167
And why did that have
to happen?

495
00:21:15,767 --> 00:21:19,533
We won't stop covering
this story

496
00:21:19,533 --> 00:21:23,200
until all those responsible
are held accountable!

497
00:21:23,200 --> 00:21:24,367
You can count on that.

498
00:21:24,367 --> 00:21:27,567
Salvador
"The Vindicator" Manalo.

499
00:21:27,567 --> 00:21:30,367
Manila Telebalita.

500
00:21:30,367 --> 00:21:32,200
That's it! Great!

501
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:33,433
- Hey!
- Hey.

502
00:21:33,433 --> 00:21:34,667
[ARNEL] That's good,
that's great.

503
00:21:34,667 --> 00:21:40,833
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

504
00:21:42,433 --> 00:21:43,500
[ISOBEL] Ricardo...

505
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:45,200
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

506
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:46,800
How's Manny?

507
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:49,733
The people at Ginintuang Lupa
filed a TRO.

508
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,233
Looks like they found
a lawyer.

509
00:21:52,233 --> 00:21:53,267
[ISOBEL EXHALES]

510
00:21:55,300 --> 00:21:57,200
Of course, they're going
to fight for that.

511
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,833
That's the only thing
they have left.

512
00:21:59,800 --> 00:22:03,533
But it's impressive
that they found an ally.

513
00:22:03,533 --> 00:22:05,400
Yeah, Isobel,
but you already know it.

514
00:22:05,400 --> 00:22:08,267
The law can be bent
so long as you have money.

515
00:22:08,267 --> 00:22:10,567
It's just a waste of their time
and resources.

516
00:22:10,567 --> 00:22:13,033
Ricardo, is--
Is this worth it?

517
00:22:14,133 --> 00:22:15,100
What?

518
00:22:15,900 --> 00:22:17,033
Everything.

519
00:22:18,133 --> 00:22:20,267
[TWINKLE] There--
Uh, ma'am!

520
00:22:20,267 --> 00:22:22,733
Ricardo. Isobel.

521
00:22:23,500 --> 00:22:26,100
I have some bad news.

522
00:22:26,100 --> 00:22:28,933
[ISOBEL] Bad news?
What is it?

523
00:22:28,933 --> 00:22:34,633
The Japanese investors
backed out of your development!

524
00:22:34,633 --> 00:22:37,133
- My god!
- No, that can't happen.

525
00:22:37,133 --> 00:22:40,267
I laid out my vision
for Ginintuang Lupa to them.

526
00:22:40,267 --> 00:22:41,433
And they liked it!

527
00:22:41,433 --> 00:22:43,467
[ISOBEL] Is this because
of what the people

528
00:22:43,467 --> 00:22:47,300
at Ginintuang Lupa did?
Those rude bastards?

529
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:50,667
[PINKY] They heard
about the demolition,

530
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:52,967
and how a lot of people
got hurt!

531
00:22:52,967 --> 00:22:56,667
They don't want to be a part
of this mess!

532
00:22:56,667 --> 00:22:58,833
Wait. I'll talk to them.

533
00:22:58,833 --> 00:23:00,333
No, I'll make them commit
to the project.

534
00:23:00,333 --> 00:23:01,333
I'll bring them back.

535
00:23:01,333 --> 00:23:04,467
They said
their decision's final.

536
00:23:04,467 --> 00:23:08,800
They don't want us
to contact them again!

537
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:11,067
[ISOBEL] Ah, Ricardo...

538
00:23:12,633 --> 00:23:15,967
Why don't we just sell
Ginintuang Lupa?

539
00:23:15,967 --> 00:23:19,700
Doesn't matter if we lose money,
or earn little.

540
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:22,267
Let's just get rid
of this problem!

541
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:25,633
Isobel, it's not that easy
to sell land.

542
00:23:25,633 --> 00:23:27,633
Pinky was trying for how long.

543
00:23:27,633 --> 00:23:30,000
She's wanted to get rid of it
for a long time now!

544
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:31,333
But no one wanted it!

545
00:23:31,333 --> 00:23:32,533
I'm the only one
who came forward

546
00:23:32,533 --> 00:23:35,967
because, as I said,
we have influence.

547
00:23:35,967 --> 00:23:41,000
I mean, I'll solve any problem
the development will face.

548
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,500
But, come on!

549
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:45,833
I didn't expect this
to be the reaction

550
00:23:45,833 --> 00:23:47,667
of the people
at Ginintuang Lupa.

551
00:23:47,667 --> 00:23:51,033
It's very difficult to resell
that property.

552
00:23:51,033 --> 00:23:54,133
Why don't we look
for investors?

553
00:23:54,133 --> 00:23:55,833
Let's focus on that instead!

554
00:23:55,867 --> 00:23:59,333
Pinky, what investors are
you talking about?

555
00:23:59,333 --> 00:24:01,733
The peso's down!

556
00:24:01,733 --> 00:24:04,700
The government's already
in turmoil.

557
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:08,067
What investors can we get
at this time?!

558
00:24:08,067 --> 00:24:09,700
I will try to find a way.

559
00:24:09,700 --> 00:24:11,567
I'll try to talk
to some people.

560
00:24:11,567 --> 00:24:17,867
Isobel, the development
of Ginintuang Lupa will happen.

561
00:24:17,867 --> 00:24:20,067
Remember, I was raised
not to fail.

562
00:24:22,367 --> 00:24:24,000
And I don't intend to start now.

563
00:24:32,567 --> 00:24:33,533
[DOOR OPENS]

564
00:24:33,633 --> 00:24:35,033
[EXHALES SOFTLY]

565
00:24:35,133 --> 00:24:40,100
- [SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]
- [DOORS OPEN]

566
00:24:40,267 --> 00:24:43,567
Doc, how's Papa doing?

567
00:24:43,700 --> 00:24:45,767
The patient's condition
is critical.

568
00:24:45,933 --> 00:24:47,367
He needs surgery right away.

569
00:24:47,467 --> 00:24:50,567
If we don't do it soon,
his lungs could collapse,

570
00:24:50,700 --> 00:24:54,733
oxygen won't reach his brain,
and it could cost him his life.

571
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:57,400
Don't worry, Doc.

572
00:24:57,533 --> 00:24:59,067
I'll find a way right now

573
00:24:59,233 --> 00:25:01,067
to get my father
into surgery immediately.

574
00:25:01,233 --> 00:25:02,400
Understood.

575
00:25:10,900 --> 00:25:17,733
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [HEART MONITOR BEEPING]

576
00:25:26,300 --> 00:25:29,467
<i> Pa, please hold on tight.</i>

577
00:25:30,833 --> 00:25:33,600
<i>I'm doing everything I can
so you'll get better soon.</i>

578
00:25:35,133 --> 00:25:39,300
<i> When I come back, I promise...</i>

579
00:25:40,333 --> 00:25:41,933
...I'll bring the money we need.

580
00:25:43,433 --> 00:25:45,600
<i>I won't let anything
happen to you, Pa.</i>

581
00:25:47,100 --> 00:25:49,400
<i>I'll do whatever it takes
to see you wake up again.</i>

582
00:25:50,667 --> 00:25:52,733
<i>Even if I have to risk
my very own life...</i>

583
00:25:54,167 --> 00:25:56,900
<i>I won't let anything bad
befall you, Pa.</i>

584
00:25:57,000 --> 00:26:03,800
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

585
00:26:12,133 --> 00:26:17,033
[HEART MONITOR BEEPING]

586
00:26:17,133 --> 00:26:20,167
<i>Crowds are everywhere,
it's Chinese New Year.</i>

587
00:26:20,300 --> 00:26:22,200
<i>Gabo sure gives us
rough assignments, huh?</i>

588
00:26:22,333 --> 00:26:24,867
<i>We're supposed to track down
someone we've never even met.</i>

589
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:28,767
<i>Mariano and I worked so hard
to build all of this up.</i>

590
00:26:28,900 --> 00:26:32,100
<i>So I want you
to prioritize the business.</i>

591
00:26:32,233 --> 00:26:34,300
Every player's
got their own plan...

592
00:26:34,467 --> 00:26:36,667
(In Cantonese)<i> Wishing you
</i> a happy, prosperous New Year!

593
00:26:36,800 --> 00:26:37,967
What a smell! Who just farted?!

594
00:26:38,133 --> 00:26:39,333
<i>Daboy,
give us a heads-up next time!</i>

595
00:26:39,467 --> 00:26:41,767
<i> - That wasn't me, come on!
</i>- It's all over my clothes too!

596
00:26:41,900 --> 00:26:44,033
Who will strike first?

597
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:45,500
<i>Get inside and run
surveillance on the place.</i>

598
00:26:45,667 --> 00:26:47,300
<i> Is your boss here?</i>

599
00:26:47,433 --> 00:26:48,967
<i>Ma'am, do you really think
we can pull this off?</i>

600
00:26:49,067 --> 00:26:50,467
<i>This case we're handling
is way too heavy.</i>

601
00:26:50,567 --> 00:26:52,833
<i>- That won't be an issue.
- We'll follow Mr. Chan,</i>

602
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:56,133
<i>he'll lead us straight
to Tiger.</i>
